  svg: '<svg class="ecg-svg ecg-paper ecg-tall" viewBox="0 0 640 610" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false" preserveAspectRatio="xMidYMid meet"><title>Fifth Universal Definition measured ECG examples</title><text class="ecg-lead" x="16" y="22">FIFTH UDMI (2026) · NEW J-POINT STE IN ≥2 CONTIGUOUS LEADS</text><text class="ecg-label ecg-label-b" x="16" y="40">Teaching schematics at standard gain · do not apply these millimetre cut-points unchanged in LBBB, paced rhythm, or LVH</text><line class="ecg-sep" x1="0" y1="52" x2="640" y2="52"/><text class="ecg-lead" x="16" y="76">A · ≥1.0 mm IN EVERY STANDARD LEAD EXCEPT V2–V3</text><text class="ecg-label" x="16" y="94">This applies to I, aVL, II, III, aVF, V1, and V4–V6. The examples below are II + III — an inferior contiguous pair.</text><text class="ecg-label" x="28" y="118">II</text><text class="ecg-label" x="338" y="118">III</text><path class="ecg-trace" d="M48,152 H112 C117,152 118,144 120,144 C122,144 124,152 128,152 H142 L147,158 L153,130 L159,156 L164,142 Q178,142 188,134 Q198,126 210,134 L218,142 H286"/><path class="ecg-trace" d="M358,152 H422 C427,152 428,144 430,144 C432,144 434,152 438,152 H452 L457,158 L463,130 L469,156 L474,142 Q488,142 498,134 Q508,126 520,134 L528,142 H596"/><circle class="ecg-j" data-wave="inf" cx="164" cy="142" r="3"><title>J point</title></circle><circle class="ecg-j" data-wave="inf" cx="474" cy="142" r="3"><title>J point</title></circle><line class="ecg-marker" data-wave="inf" x1="230" y1="142" x2="230" y2="152"/><line class="ecg-marker" data-wave="inf" x1="540" y1="142" x2="540" y2="152"/><text class="ecg-label ecg-label-b" data-wave="inf" x="178" y="174">STE 1.0 mm</text><text class="ecg-label ecg-label-b" data-wave="inf" x="488" y="174">STE 1.0 mm</text><text class="ecg-label" x="28" y="194">One lead alone is insufficient: pair the electrical change with an anatomically contiguous lead and the clinical syndrome.</text><line class="ecg-sep" x1="0" y1="208" x2="640" y2="208"/><text class="ecg-lead" x="16" y="232">B · V2–V3 ARE THE ONLY STANDARD-LEAD SEX/AGE EXCEPTION</text><text class="ecg-label" x="28" y="254">V2–V3: men &lt;40 years</text><text class="ecg-label" x="238" y="254">men ≥40 years</text><text class="ecg-label" x="444" y="254">women, any age</text><path class="ecg-trace" d="M28,300 H72 C77,300 78,292 80,292 C82,292 84,300 88,300 H100 L105,306 L111,272 L117,304 L122,275 Q136,275 146,262 Q156,250 168,262 L176,275 H214"/><path class="ecg-trace" d="M234,300 H278 C283,300 284,292 286,292 C288,292 290,300 294,300 H306 L311,306 L317,272 L323,304 L328,280 Q342,280 352,270 Q362,260 374,270 L382,280 H420"/><path class="ecg-trace" d="M440,300 H484 C489,300 490,292 492,292 C494,292 496,300 500,300 H512 L517,306 L523,272 L529,304 L534,285 Q548,285 558,277 Q568,270 580,277 L588,285 H626"/><circle class="ecg-j" data-wave="ant" cx="122" cy="275" r="3"><title>J point</title></circle><circle class="ecg-j" data-wave="ant" cx="328" cy="280" r="3"><title>J point</title></circle><circle class="ecg-j" data-wave="ant" cx="534" cy="285" r="3"><title>J point</title></circle><line class="ecg-marker" data-wave="ant" x1="184" y1="275" x2="184" y2="300"/><line class="ecg-marker" data-wave="ant" x1="390" y1="280" x2="390" y2="300"/><line class="ecg-marker" data-wave="ant" x1="608" y1="285" x2="608" y2="300"/><text class="ecg-label ecg-label-b" data-wave="ant" x="84" y="324">≥2.5 mm</text><text class="ecg-label ecg-label-b" data-wave="ant" x="290" y="324">≥2.0 mm</text><text class="ecg-label ecg-label-b" data-wave="ant" x="496" y="324">≥1.5 mm</text><text class="ecg-label" x="28" y="344">The same threshold applies to both V2 and V3; still require a contiguous pair and a compatible clinical presentation.</text><line class="ecg-sep" x1="0" y1="358" x2="640" y2="358"/><text class="ecg-lead" x="16" y="382">C · RECORD THE LEADS THAT ANSWER THE CLINICAL QUESTION</text><text class="ecg-label" x="28" y="404">V4R — RV involvement with inferior injury</text><text class="ecg-label" x="338" y="404">V1–V3 mirror → record V7–V9 posterior leads</text><path class="ecg-trace" d="M28,442 H82 C87,442 88,434 90,434 C92,434 94,442 98,442 H112 L117,448 L123,420 L129,446 L134,437 Q148,437 158,430 Q168,423 180,430 L188,437 H282"/><circle class="ecg-j" data-wave="inf" cx="134" cy="437" r="3"><title>J point</title></circle><line class="ecg-marker" data-wave="inf" x1="204" y1="437" x2="204" y2="442"/><text class="ecg-label ecg-label-b" data-wave="inf" x="48" y="464">V4R STE ≥0.5 mm supports RV infarction</text><text class="ecg-label" x="48" y="480">≥1.0 mm for men &lt;30 years</text><path class="ecg-trace" d="M338,442 H382 C387,442 388,434 390,434 C392,434 394,442 398,442 H412 L417,448 L423,420 L429,446 L434,452 Q448,452 458,462 Q468,472 480,462 L488,452 H514 H514,442 C519,442 520,434 522,434 C524,434 526,442 530,442 H544 L549,448 L555,420 L561,446 L566,437 Q580,437 590,430 Q600,423 612,430 L620,437 H634"/><line class="ecg-marker" data-wave="post" x1="470" y1="442" x2="470" y2="452"/><line class="ecg-marker" data-wave="post" x1="600" y1="437" x2="600" y2="442"/><text class="ecg-label ecg-label-b" data-wave="post" x="348" y="464">V2: horizontal STD ≥1 mm → V8: STE ≥0.5 mm</text><text class="ecg-label" x="348" y="480">V7 posterior axillary · V8 mid-scapular · V9 left paraspinal, V6 horizontal plane</text><line class="ecg-sep" x1="0" y1="494" x2="640" y2="494"/><text class="ecg-lead" x="16" y="518">D · ISCHEMIA MAY NOT HAVE CLASSIC STE</text><path class="ecg-trace" d="M28,556 H82 C87,556 88,548 90,548 C92,548 94,556 98,556 H112 L117,562 L123,534 L129,560 L134,562 Q148,562 158,584 Q168,598 180,584 L188,562 H238 H238,556 C243,556 244,548 246,548 C248,548 250,556 254,556 H268 L273,562 L279,534 L285,560 L290,562 Q304,562 314,584 Q324,598 336,584 L344,562 H390"/><text class="ecg-label ecg-label-b" data-wave="ischa" x="28" y="602">Two contiguous leads: new horizontal/downsloping STD ≥0.5 mm, dynamic TWI ≥1 mm, or broad hyperacute T waves can be ischemic.</text><text class="ecg-label" data-wave="ischa" x="28" y="618">Compare a prior ECG and repeat with ongoing symptoms; an occlusion pattern does not wait for a millimetre label.</text><g class="ecg-hots"><g class="ecg-hot" tabindex="0" role="button" data-wave="inf" aria-label="Standard-lead ST elevation: 1 millimetre in each of two contiguous inferior leads. The 1 millimetre rule applies to standard leads other than V2 and V3."><rect x="24" y="110" width="576" height="82" rx="6" class="ecg-hotzone"/><title>Standard-lead 1 millimetre threshold</title></g><g class="ecg-hot" tabindex="0" role="button" data-wave="ant" aria-label="V2 and V3 sex and age cut-points: 2.5 millimetres in men under 40, 2.0 millimetres in men 40 or older, and 1.5 millimetres in women."><rect x="20" y="244" width="612" height="104" rx="6" class="ecg-hotzone"/><title>V2 V3 sex-age exception</title></g><g class="ecg-hot" tabindex="0" role="button" data-wave="post" aria-label="Supplemental leads: V4R for right ventricular involvement and V7 through V9 for posterior infarction."><rect x="20" y="394" width="612" height="92" rx="6" class="ecg-hotzone"/><title>Right-sided and posterior leads</title></g><g class="ecg-hot" tabindex="0" role="button" data-wave="ischa" aria-label="Contiguous ST depression and dynamic T-wave inversion are ischemic changes beyond classic ST elevation."><rect x="20" y="528" width="380" height="78" rx="6" class="ecg-hotzone"/><title>Ischemia without classic ST elevation</title></g></g></svg>'
